{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790356608,"nonce":"okkGzyh5ehfdsCHH4bjxTkcfG+E=","title":"Lua resume_points: a_region_taking_a_number_aggregate_runs_on_llvm no longer reaches an outlined region","message":"The test (crates/zyntax_lua/tests/resume_points.rs, fixture tests/fixtures/number_region.lua) asserts that lua$main$1$resume0, a region outlined for an interpreted frame, is recompiled at tier 1. Now main() is compiled at the baseline before its loop gets hot, its compiled frame asks for promotion at the probe, the whole function is promoted to LLVM and the frame transfers at the late resume point. Output is correct; only the region path the test pins is not taken.\n\nSeen 10 of 10 runs with main 588a2748's release zylua (ZYLUA_LLVM=1 ZYNTAX_OSR_TRACE=1), 10 of 10 with a debug build of the batch on top of it, and in the 5ee91b7 verifier's run on d7500d72 plus 5ee91b7. The earlier main run of this suite stopped at a conformance failure before reaching resume_points, so this went unnoticed. df43c347 (quick baseline's promotion waits for its replacement) is the likely point where the frame stopped being interpreted; not bisected.\n\nThe test needs a fixture that keeps the frame interpreted when the loop gets hot (for example a main chunk loop, or ZYNTAX_DISABLE_WARM_UP), so the aggregate-by-address region ABI stays covered.","files":null}]}